# i18n Conventions

## Usage

```tsx
import { useI18n } from '@/locale';

const { t, locale, setLocale } = useI18n();
return <h2>{t('section.title')}</h2>;
```

## Adding strings

1. Add the same key to **both** `src/locale/en.json` and `src/locale/zh.json`
2. Use dot-notation keys grouped by section (e.g. `hero.subtitle`, `skills.title`)
3. Missing keys fall back to the key string — always add both locales

## Locale switching

- `setLocale('en')` or `setLocale('zh')`
- Selection persists in `localStorage` under `app_locale`
- Header component has the locale selector

## Do not

- Hardcode user-facing strings in JSX (except proper nouns, URLs, or code)
- Add a key to only one locale file
